I've been thinking about a Sumo character class.
It may not be practical but it's an amusing idea.

The character starts with no weapons or armor... or maybe
a piece of armor that has no AC benefit, like a mummy wrapping.
Maybe a bit of food (chanko-nabe?).

Strength and constitution are high, I suppose, although I know
that's a bit of a yawn.  Pretty high dex too.  Low charisma
starting out.

The sumo character has two special attacks: grabbing and crushing
(like pit fiends and owlbears) and swallowing (like purple worms).
Maybe grabbing and crushing should not be attained until level 7
or so.
I think this would only be a slight advantage.  It takes a couple
of successful attacks to be able to grab a creature; and then the
crushing attack only lasts as long as you don't move away from the
creature or attack something else.  But it would be an interesting
option.

Swallowing monsters is limited by the character's capacity to eat.
However, I think the Sumo character should have a higher metabolism
than the usual character; the character would have to eat more in
order to stay alive.  Basically the same as an intrinsic ring of
hunger.  As long as there are edible monsters around, this is good,
but would be a challenge otherwise.  It would also be realistic for
the Sumo to have a greater eating capacity, i.e., it would take more
food rations to go from fainting to satiated.  But maybe this would be
weighing the scales (no pun intended) too heavily in the Sumo's favor.

To keep realistic limitations, it seems that swallowing a poisonous
creature should cause poison damage just like eating that creature's
corpse would.  But this doesn't seem to be the case, when I tried it
as a trapper in debug mode.  :-(

Level titles could be taken from Sumo ranks: makushita, juuryou,
maegashira #N, komosubi, sekiwake, ozeki, yokozuna, oya___
(stablemaster -- what's the word?).

I don't know what the letter for the class would be.
'S'umo, 'R'ikishi, and 'W'restler all clash with other classes.
Maybe 'U'.

